there's been a lot of talk about  recession lately recession 2023 24. i  think there are a lot of people that  think we're currently in a recession i'm  not predicting the end of the world or  an immediate recession but the road  ahead does not look great we've gotten  warnings from top wall street analysts  including deutsche bank and goldman  sachs and even former federal reserve  chairman ben bernanke has expressed  concerns about a recession the more the  fed has to tighten in order to get  inflation down the bigger the chance of  a recession and the more severe it will  be but what does it all mean and what  can we even do about it i'm gonna tell  you how economists know when a recession  has happened point out some economic  indicators that have done a good job of  historically predicting recessions and  tell you what three things average  americans can do in case recession is  coming  let's get into it should americans be  prepared for a recession recessions are  painful they typically involve  widespread job losses increased hunger  and homelessness and even higher death  rates so the question of whether the u.s  economy is really headed into a  recession is an important one officially  a recession is a significant decline in  economic activity that is spread across  the economy and lasts more than a few  months  a u.s recession is determined by  economists at the national bureau for  economic research they look at the  country's economic growth during a  period of time and decide after the fact  whether a recession has started and when  that means there's literally no way to  know for sure that we're in a recession  until after it has been declared that  said there are some solid economic  reports that have historically been  reliable indicators the first is the  inversion of the u.s treasury yield  curve that happened in march and  recessions are typically declared  between 6 and 24 months after check out  my video from earlier this year for more  details on the yield curve and its  ability to predict recessions big name  discount retailers have also painted a  gloomy picture with burlington walmart  and ross all writing down their outlooks  for this year another widely followed  recession predictor is the conference  board's leading economic index the index  is made up of 10 data points that  include employment housing business  orders and markets put together they  have a pretty strong track record of  predicting recessions the index has been  negative twice so far this year  including the most recent reading and  over the all important six month period  the index is flattening out a clear sign  of an economic slowdown ottoman ozil  dirham senior director for economics at  the conference board tells me the  reading suggests we've entered a  different type of economic environment  and are likely at an inflection point  that suggests a slowing of growth but  ozodirum also notes that in terms of  calling a recession we're not there yet  the index would need to fall further and  we'd need to see economic weakness  showing in more of the data but if the  worst is still to come what can you do  about it well the first step is being  prepared that doesn't mean pulling  everything out of your 401k and burying  cash in the backyard it means making a  plan here's three simple things you can  do today first start a savings account  if you don't have one next put together  a budget of your monthly expenses and  find places where you can save  finally create a spreadsheet that  details how much money you would need in  the event of a job loss or financial  emergency and work to put that money  aside  even if all this recession fear turns  out to be hype no one has ever regretted  having a solid budget and some extra  money in the bank the situation reminds  me of a plea from rapper young jeezy in  2008 he said interest rates are going up  seems like no value in the buck  meat price is up to stay  utilities are on their way  airlines are running late  please  let the dollar circulate  that's all for now see you next time
 

